//       _1375 (the head, y 1088)  _1422 (1120)  _1468 (1152)  _1514 (1184)
//   — hanging beneath the horizontal beam row at y 1056 (`_1322`..`_1328`),
//   with `_1374` / `_1376` as the posts on either side. An earlier version of
//   this file asserted "THERE IS NO LADDER ART IN THIS PROJECT". That was
//   false, and every claim built on it was false with it. The honest version
//   is stronger: the LOOK is one drag and one paint stroke, and the MECHANIC
//   is the whole lesson.
//   PALETTE MEMBERSHIP, checked by guid inside `Caves.prefab` (which 7.1
//   established is a Tile Palette saved as a prefab): `_1375` IS in the tray,
//   `_1328` (the beam) IS, `_1374` IS — and `_1422`, `_1468`, `_1514` and
//   `_1376` are on NEITHER palette. So the student's first move is to drag
